# VideoVault — Project Overview

## What It Is
A native macOS (cross-platform) desktop video manager built with **Tauri v2 + React + TypeScript + Vite**.
No web server — ships as a `.app` / `.dmg` installer. Launched with `cargo tauri dev`.

## Tech Stack
| Layer | Technology |
|---|---|
| UI | React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 |
| State | Zustand (with `persist` middleware) |
| Desktop shell | Tauri v2 (Rust backend, WKWebView frontend) |
| Database | SQLite via `rusqlite` (bundled) |
| Video processing | FFmpeg (resolved via `ffmpeg_bin()` helper — always use this, never `Command::new("ffmpeg")` directly) |
| AI tagging | OpenAI / Anthropic / Google Gemini / Ollama (selectable in Settings) |

## Key Directories
```
src/                  React frontend
  components/         UI components (Player, VideoGrid, TagModal, MergeModal, etc.)
  store/index.ts      Single Zustand store — all global state
  types/index.ts      Shared TypeScript types
  lib/utils.ts        Helpers: cn(), formatDuration(), getThumbnailSrc(), getVideoSrc()
src-tauri/src/
  lib.rs              App entry — registers all Tauri commands
  commands.rs         All #[tauri::command] handlers
  db.rs               SQLite schema + helpers
  ffmpeg.rs           FFmpeg wrapper (probe, thumbnail, merge, trim)
  llm.rs              LLM provider abstraction
  llm_commands.rs     Auto-tag Tauri commands
```

## Critical Conventions

### File paths → URLs
Always use `convertFileSrc(path)` or `getThumbnailSrc(path)` (which wraps it) for local file URLs.
Never use `asset://${path}` directly — it produces the wrong format on macOS.

### Tauri IPC timing (dev only)
All `invoke()` and `listen()` calls in `useEffect` must be deferred by 50ms to avoid firing before `__TAURI__` is injected after HMR reloads:
```tsx
useEffect(() => {
  const t = setTimeout(() => invoke('...').catch(console.warn), 50)
  return () => clearTimeout(t)
}, [])
```

### FFmpeg path
In Rust, always call `ffmpeg_bin()` / `ffprobe_bin()` instead of hardcoded strings — resolves Homebrew path on macOS GUI apps where PATH is limited.

### Blocking Rust ops
Wrap sync FFmpeg calls inside async Tauri commands with `tokio::task::block_in_place(|| { ... })`.

### Asset protocol scope
`tauri.conf.json` has `assetProtocol.scope: ["$HOME/**"]` — required for WKWebView to load local video/thumbnail files.

